{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "c74dabb4-902e-5f8a-a4c6-401f45cc8254",
    "name": "nest-ai-starter labs",
    "description": "Every REST and MCP call the course labs make.\n\n1. In boilerplate/nest-ai-starter: `pnpm build && pnpm db:migrate && pnpm start`.\n2. Import this file into Postman. `baseUrl` is http://localhost:3000.\n3. Run the folders in order (or the whole collection with the Runner).\n\nFolders are numbered by chapter; each name also says its module.\n\nAuth: \"Log in\" (folder 03) trades {{email}} / {{password}} (a local demo user) for a token; the collection then sends `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}`. Requests that must not send it override it. MCP requests authenticate as a device with X-Device-Key / X-Device-Secret.\n\nSECRETS. Provisioning stores the device secret in the `secret` variable (current value). Never export, share or commit the collection after running it. Re-import the clean file instead.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000"
    },
    {
      "key": "email",
      "value": "demo@example.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "demo passphrase for labs"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "deviceId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "deviceKey",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "secret",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "rotatedSecret",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "noteId",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "id": "b06f2ece-5d26-5cfb-8384-858826298676",
      "name": "00 · Setup (module 1)",
      "description": "Is the app up? Run this first.",
      "item": [
        {
          "id": "ece7d0de-9e82-5a31-ba43-5c258bb360f1",
          "name": "Health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "health"]
            },
            "description": "Unversioned and public. 200 `{\"status\":\"ok\"}` once migrate has run and the app has started.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 ok', () => { pm.response.to.have.status(200); pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('ok'); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "99629e77-1f64-53bf-b4ff-59aa5d589d19",
      "name": "03 · Auth (module 3)",
      "description": "Sign up, log in with Basic to get a token, then use the token. Every failure is the same 401. Chapter 03 lab: give unknown emails a different message at login and re-run this folder: the \"same body\" test fails, and so does the e2e test that pins the rule.",
      "item": [
        {
          "id": "ee807d98-a9ce-5d7a-8fd0-d9c7fb2302a8",
          "name": "Sign up (public)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "users"]
            },
            "description": "The one public write. 201 creates the user; 409 means it already exists, which is fine for a re-run. Chapter 02 lab: once you add `phone`, add it to this body.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"name\": \"Demo\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 created, or 409 already exists', () => { pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([201, 409]); });",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  const u = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.test('no password or hash in the response', () => { pm.expect(u).to.not.have.any.keys('password', 'passwordHash'); });",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c445ba1d-6aac-5790-848e-7dc6869aeb7f",
          "name": "Log in: wrong password → 401",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "A known email with a wrong password.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "basic",
              "basic": [
                {
                  "key": "username",
                  "value": "{{email}}",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "key": "password",
                  "value": "not-the-password",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401 with a Basic challenge', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('WWW-Authenticate')).to.include('Basic');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('the same body as every other auth failure', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.eql({ statusCode: 401, error: 'Unauthorized', message: 'Invalid credentials' });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "fb8ad5f9-81bd-50fc-be9f-9f5496d7c284",
          "name": "Log in: unknown email → the same 401",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "An email nobody registered. Same 401 again, so emails cannot be probed.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "basic",
              "basic": [
                {
                  "key": "username",
                  "value": "nobody@example.com",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "key": "password",
                  "value": "{{password}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401 with a Basic challenge', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('WWW-Authenticate')).to.include('Basic');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('the same body as every other auth failure', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.eql({ statusCode: 401, error: 'Unauthorized', message: 'Invalid credentials' });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ffe1b2bb-a44a-509a-9b7d-b991606873f9",
          "name": "Log in (Basic) → token",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Basic with {{email}} / {{password}}. The test stores the access token in the `token` variable; every later request sends it as `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}` (the collection auth).",
            "auth": {
              "type": "basic",
              "basic": [
                {
                  "key": "username",
                  "value": "{{email}}",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "key": "password",
                  "value": "{{password}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 with a bearer token', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const t = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(t.tokenType).to.eql('Bearer');",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', t.accessToken);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "39b12d57-57a0-52fc-8b0e-97200f3d5c26",
          "name": "Me: no token → 401",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "me"]
            },
            "description": "No Authorization header at all.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401 with a Bearer challenge', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('WWW-Authenticate')).to.include('Bearer');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('the same body as every other auth failure', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.eql({ statusCode: 401, error: 'Unauthorized', message: 'Invalid credentials' });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "a22968c4-80cc-5206-a4d0-acde800f5cfc",
          "name": "Me (Bearer token)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Uses the collection auth: Bearer {{token}}."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200, the public user', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const u = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(u.email).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('email'));",
                  "  pm.expect(u).to.not.have.any.keys('password', 'passwordHash');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "9bc82436-4612-520f-8d4c-ec49aa84ede0",
      "name": "04 · Devices (module 3)",
      "description": "Provision a device: one call creates it and returns its key and secret (the secret is shown ONCE and stored in the `secret` variable). Then read it back: the secret never appears again.",
      "item": [
        {
          "id": "6432d43c-a84a-57d4-b5b7-69c66e8ae84f",
          "name": "Provision device (key + secret shown once)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/devices/provision",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "devices", "provision"]
            },
            "description": "Owned by the signed-in user, active at once. Returns `deviceKey` and the plaintext `secret`, ONCE. The test stores both in collection variables. Never paste the secret anywhere, and never share or export the collection with its current values.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"postman device\",\n  \"description\": \"created from the Postman collection\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201, an active device with a key and a one-time secret', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "  const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(d.status).to.eql('active');",
                  "  pm.expect(d.deviceKey).to.match(/^DK[A-Z2-7]{16}$/);",
                  "  pm.expect(d.secret).to.match(/^dsk_/);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('deviceId', d.id);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('deviceKey', d.deviceKey);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('secret', d.secret);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "184c39d7-67fa-5b1d-bb60-b2e07b1c4f01",
          "name": "Get device (no secret, no hash)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/devices/{{deviceId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "devices", "{{deviceId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Chapter 04 checkpoint: only provision and rotate ever show a secret."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200, secret and hash never returned', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(d).to.not.have.any.keys('secret', 'secretHash');",
                  "  pm.expect(d.deviceKey).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('deviceKey'));",
                  "  pm.expect(d.secretLast4).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('secret').slice(-4));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "e371eb20-7431-57f0-8c5b-a65d25b9ced4",
          "name": "List my devices",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/devices",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "devices"]
            },
            "description": "Only the signed-in user's devices. Another user's device id answers 404, never 403."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "47719d02-1eb8-57a8-8de2-d75fedf39b69",
      "name": "05 · MCP over HTTP (module 5)",
      "description": "Raw JSON-RPC to /mcp (the device headers matter from module 6 on). The server is stateless: every POST stands alone, and the answer is one SSE `message` event. Read the Body tab: `event: message` then `data: {...}`.",
      "item": [
        {
          "id": "d0b32d19-d0cd-5f81-9ad0-999df3f36a69",
          "name": "initialize",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Device-Key",
                "value": "{{deviceKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Device-Secret",
                "value": "{{secret}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["mcp"]
            },
            "description": "Chapter 05: match the response `id` to the request `id`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"method\": \"initialize\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"protocolVersion\": \"2025-06-18\",\n    \"capabilities\": {},\n    \"clientInfo\": {\n      \"name\": \"postman\",\n      \"version\": \"1\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const rpc = () => { const t = pm.response.text(); const d = t.split('\\n').find((l) => l.startsWith('data: ')); return JSON.parse(d ? d.slice(6) : t); };",
                  "pm.test('200 SSE with the matching id', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('text/event-stream');",
                  "  const m = rpc();",
                  "  pm.expect(m.id).to.eql(1);",
                  "  pm.expect(m.result.serverInfo.name).to.eql('nest-ai-starter');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b4d59d99-1227-5a89-a9d4-b44119e1f9b1",
          "name": "tools/list",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Device-Key",
                "value": "{{deviceKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Device-Secret",
                "value": "{{secret}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["mcp"]
            },
            "description": "The tools this server exposes. Chapter 06 lab: after you add publish-note, it appears here.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 2,\n  \"method\": \"tools/list\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const rpc = () => { const t = pm.response.text(); const d = t.split('\\n').find((l) => l.startsWith('data: ')); return JSON.parse(d ? d.slice(6) : t); };",
                  "pm.test('lists the tools', () => {",
                  "  const names = rpc().result.tools.map((t) => t.name);",
                  "  pm.expect(names).to.include.members(['create-note', 'get-note', 'list-notes', 'whoami']);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c0e06eb5-7ae2-581a-a3e0-a54869c671fb",
          "name": "tools/call whoami",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Device-Key",
                "value": "{{deviceKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Device-Secret",
                "value": "{{secret}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["mcp"]
            },
            "description": "Who is calling: the device and its owner, resolved from the X-Device-Key / X-Device-Secret headers.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 3,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"whoami\",\n    \"arguments\": {}\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const rpc = () => { const t = pm.response.text(); const d = t.split('\\n').find((l) => l.startsWith('data: ')); return JSON.parse(d ? d.slice(6) : t); };",
                  "pm.test('the active device and its owner', () => {",
                  "  const r = rpc().result;",
                  "  pm.expect(r.isError).to.not.eql(true);",
                  "  const text = r.content[0].text;",
                  "  pm.expect(text).to.include(pm.collectionVariables.get('email'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "aaf2cecd-fc0b-5ba6-8822-54179254de29",
          "name": "tools/call create-note (empty published → tool error)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Device-Key",
                "value": "{{deviceKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Device-Secret",
                "value": "{{secret}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["mcp"]
            },
            "description": "A rule violation comes back as a TOOL error (`isError: true`, readable by the model), not a protocol error. Chapter 07 lab: this is the input your CI check must reject.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 4,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"create-note\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"title\": \"from postman\",\n      \"status\": \"published\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const rpc = () => { const t = pm.response.text(); const d = t.split('\\n').find((l) => l.startsWith('data: ')); return JSON.parse(d ? d.slice(6) : t); };",
                  "pm.test('isError, not a JSON-RPC error', () => {",
                  "  const m = rpc();",
                  "  pm.expect(m.error).to.be.undefined;",
                  "  pm.expect(m.result.isError).to.eql(true);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "350cf546-ecf0-5b89-8fb4-1c70759eeda5",
          "name": "tools/call create-note",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Device-Key",
                "value": "{{deviceKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Device-Secret",
                "value": "{{secret}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["mcp"]
            },
            "description": "A valid note. The result text carries the note as JSON.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 5,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"create-note\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"title\": \"from postman\",\n      \"body\": \"created over MCP\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const rpc = () => { const t = pm.response.text(); const d = t.split('\\n').find((l) => l.startsWith('data: ')); return JSON.parse(d ? d.slice(6) : t); };",
                  "pm.test('created', () => { pm.expect(rpc().result.isError).to.not.eql(true); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "924e9bef-441e-5a84-ae10-d319f6d75571",
          "name": "No device headers → 401",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["mcp"]
            },
            "description": "Device auth runs BEFORE the MCP transport. Missing, wrong, archived or rotated: all the same 401.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 6,\n  \"method\": \"ping\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const rpc = () => { const t = pm.response.text(); const d = t.split('\\n').find((l) => l.startsWith('data: ')); return JSON.parse(d ? d.slice(6) : t); };",
                  "pm.test('401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0d11c25c-281e-5481-84bc-9cd065be4360",
      "name": "06 · Notes over REST (module 4)",
      "description": "The same rule as the MCP tool, at the HTTP boundary: a published note needs a non-empty body.",
      "item": [
        {
          "id": "48a07907-501c-5e7d-962a-1bf09b74a686",
          "name": "Create note (draft, empty body)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notes",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "notes"]
            },
            "description": "Defaults: status `draft`, body empty.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"from postman\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 draft', () => { pm.response.to.have.status(201); pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('draft'); });",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('noteId', pm.response.json().id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "f05b20a3-9f7e-5d86-89fc-0d5a7044d009",
          "name": "Publish it → 422 RULE_VIOLATION",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notes/{{noteId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "notes", "{{noteId}}"]
            },
            "description": "A rule that needs stored state lives in the service and answers 422. Delete the rule in the service and this test goes red: that is the chapter 01 mutation check.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"published\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('422 rule violation', () => { pm.response.to.have.status(422); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "51e63642-2352-580e-be76-ab42e5eba3e2",
          "name": "Get note",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notes/{{noteId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "notes", "{{noteId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Still a draft."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 still draft', () => { pm.response.to.have.status(200); pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('draft'); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "acfab4f9-73c0-5c58-8e49-1b45fa8efb69",
      "name": "08 · Host check (module 5)",
      "description": "DNS-rebinding protection: a Host that is not in MCP_ALLOWED_HOSTS gets 403 even with valid credentials. Postman lets you override Host; fetch() in a test silently does not.",
      "item": [
        {
          "id": "15562283-2a1b-5ffe-8bad-2ac3c5b9fcaa",
          "name": "Foreign Host → 403",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Device-Key",
                "value": "{{deviceKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Device-Secret",
                "value": "{{secret}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Host",
                "value": "evil.example"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["mcp"]
            },
            "description": "Valid device headers, Host set to evil.example.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 7,\n  \"method\": \"ping\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const rpc = () => { const t = pm.response.text(); const d = t.split('\\n').find((l) => l.startsWith('data: ')); return JSON.parse(d ? d.slice(6) : t); };",
                  "pm.test('403', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "97b69aca-d1e1-50fe-9a35-4e6427e8e991",
      "name": "09 · Rotate mid-session (module 6)",
      "description": "Rotate the secret, then call whoami with the OLD one: it fails at once. The new one works.",
      "item": [
        {
          "id": "21d50adf-351e-5d32-adca-6e24cadbf021",
          "name": "Rotate secret",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/devices/{{deviceId}}/rotate",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "devices", "{{deviceId}}", "rotate"]
            },
            "description": "Same deviceKey, new secret. The OLD secret stays in `secret` for the next request; the new one goes to `rotatedSecret`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('same key, new secret', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const c = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(c.deviceKey).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('deviceKey'));",
                  "  pm.expect(c.secret).to.not.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('secret'));",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('rotatedSecret', c.secret);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "6cba0e96-f95b-5112-9371-b236e292bd2e",
          "name": "whoami with the OLD secret → 401",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Device-Key",
                "value": "{{deviceKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Device-Secret",
                "value": "{{secret}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["mcp"]
            },
            "description": "The rotation took effect on the very next call. The test first checks that a rotation really happened: with no device at all this call is 401 too, and a check that passes by doing nothing proves nothing.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 8,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"whoami\",\n    \"arguments\": {}\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const rpc = () => { const t = pm.response.text(); const d = t.split('\\n').find((l) => l.startsWith('data: ')); return JSON.parse(d ? d.slice(6) : t); };",
                  "pm.test('a rotation ran first (Rotate credentials stored a new secret)', () => pm.expect(pm.collectionVariables.get('rotatedSecret')).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "pm.test('401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "64bcbdca-36bc-5e89-b1d2-80c16825c883",
          "name": "whoami with the NEW secret",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Device-Key",
                "value": "{{deviceKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Device-Secret",
                "value": "{{rotatedSecret}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["mcp"]
            },
            "description": "Uses `rotatedSecret`, then promotes it to `secret`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 9,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"whoami\",\n    \"arguments\": {}\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const rpc = () => { const t = pm.response.text(); const d = t.split('\\n').find((l) => l.startsWith('data: ')); return JSON.parse(d ? d.slice(6) : t); };",
                  "pm.test('200 and not a tool error', () => { pm.response.to.have.status(200); pm.expect(rpc().result.isError).to.not.eql(true); });",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('secret', pm.collectionVariables.get('rotatedSecret'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('rotatedSecret', '');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
